<title>FRANCE: Egyptair takes delivery of Airbus A321.</title>
<headline>Egyptair takes delivery of Airbus A321.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airbus Industrie said on Saturday that Egyptair had taken delivery of the first of four Airbus A321 planes on order.</p>
<p>The A321 is a stretched version of the A320.</p>
<p>Airbus said in a statement that deliveries of the A320 family now stand at some 670 aircraft to more than 60 customers.</p>
<p>Airbus is a Toulouse-based consortium of France's Aerospatiale, Daimler-Benz Aerospace (DASA), British Aerospace and Construcciones Aeronauticas (CASA) of Spain.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
